From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:31:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zram_swap.service: Read the RAM size from /proc/meminfo

The unit sizes the swap device from "free -m". BusyBox free ignores -m
and prints KiB, so on a BusyBox system the device is requested 1024
times too large (110880 MB on a 216 MiB machine). The kernel cannot
allocate it and zram-init fails with "cannot set zram0 size".

Take MemTotal from /proc/meminfo, which is in KiB everywhere, and halve
it into MiB. This also drops the dependency on procps.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
---
 systemd/system/zram_swap.service | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/systemd/system/zram_swap.service b/systemd/system/zram_swap.service
index 99aae6e..19afea5 100644
--- a/systemd/system/zram_swap.service
+++ b/systemd/system/zram_swap.service
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ RemainAfterExit=true
 # zram_tmp.service and zram_var_tmp.service and that
 # num_devices in modprobe.d/zram.conf contains the maximal used number + 1
 
-ExecStart=/bin/sh -c "exec /sbin/zram-init -azstd -Lzram_swap `LC_ALL=C free -m | awk '/^Mem:/{print int($2/2)}'`"
+ExecStart=/bin/sh -c "exec /sbin/zram-init -azstd -Lzram_swap `awk '/^MemTotal:/{print int($2/2048)}' /proc/meminfo`"
 ExecStop=/sbin/zram-init 0
 
 [Install]
